<h2>Journal Entry Aggregation overview</h2>
<p>Journal Entry Aggregation runs a batch job that prepares a summary table, and the Trial Balance Report uses that pre-baked data instead of aggregating every day. Journal entries trigger and use the same legacy events when created.</p>
<h2>Aggregation job filters</h2>
<p>The aggregation job filters journal entries by office, entry type, manual flag, and submission date relative to the latest aggregated date.</p>
<p>The post_snapshot_delta_data where clause filters acc_gl_journal_entry where:</p>
<ul>
<li>entity_type_enum equals 1</li>
<li>manual_entry equals false</li>
<li>the latest aggregated date is null or submitted_on_date is greater than the latest aggregated date</li>
<li>submitted_on_date is less than endDate</li>
<li>office_id matches the office parameter</li>
</ul>
<p>The summary_snapshot_baseline_data where clause filters ags where:</p>
<ul>
<li>entity_type_enum equals 1</li>
<li>manual_entry equals false</li>
<li>aggregated_on_date is less than or equal to the latest aggregated date</li>
<li>office_id matches the office parameter</li>
</ul>
<p>summary_snapshot_baseline_data groups results by productname, glcode, glname, and assetowner.</p>
<h2>Payment Waiver journal entries</h2>
<p>A Payment Waiver posts credits to Loan portfolio, Interest Receivable, Fees Receivable, Penalties Receivable, and Overpayment for their allocated portions on non charge-off loan accounts. On charge-off loan accounts, it debits Income from Interest and credits Income from charge-off Interest and Overpayment. Reversals post the opposite entries.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Account type</th>
<th>Transaction</th>
<th>Debit</th>
<th>Credit</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>Non charge-off</td>
<td>Payment Waiver</td>
<td>—</td>
<td>Loan portfolio (GL 112601) for total principal; Interest Receivable (GL 112603) for total interest; Fees Receivable (GL 112603) for total fees; Penalties Receivable (GL 112603) for total penalties; Overpayment for total overpayment</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Non charge-off</td>
<td>Payment Waiver reversal</td>
<td>Income from Interest (GL 404000) for total amount entered</td>
<td>Loan portfolio (GL 112601), Interest Receivable (GL 112603), Fees Receivable (GL 112603), Penalties Receivable (GL 112603), and Overpayment for their respective allocated portions</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Charge-off</td>
<td>Payment Waiver</td>
<td>Income from Interest (GL 404000) for total amount entered</td>
<td>Income from charge-off Interest (GL 404001) for total principal, interest, fees, and penalties; Overpayment for total overpayment</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Charge-off</td>
<td>Payment Waiver reversal</td>
<td>Income from charge-off Interest (GL 404001) for total principal, interest, fees, and penalties; Overpayment for total overpayment</td>
<td>Income from Interest (GL 404000) for total amount entered</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
